1
00:00:03,545 --> 00:00:06,228
So I came to CMU as a writing major.

2
00:00:06,228 --> 00:00:13,147
I decided to look into the education program once I stepped foot into a school and saw someone teaching English to these kids.

3
00:00:13,147 --> 00:00:16,255
I think I immediately knew that it was something that I wanted to do.

4
00:00:16,255 --> 00:00:19,566
The Center for Teacher Education is a professional program.

5
00:00:19,566 --> 00:00:27,202
We have several accredited programs and in broad terms that would be elementary, secondary, K through 12.

6
00:00:27,202 --> 00:00:30,483
We also have an elementary program that is fully online.

7
00:00:30,483 --> 00:00:37,600
When our students graduate, they are eligible to apply for a teaching license with the state of Colorado.

8
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:44,429
My favorite experience of the whole teacher program has been CMU's ability to get you into classrooms in District 51.

9
00:00:44,429 --> 00:00:49,486
And what's really cool about CMU is that they let you do your observations in a lot of different schools.&nbsp;

10
00:00:49,486 --> 00:00:51,144
I've been in a fifth grade classroom.

11
00:00:51,144 --> 00:00:52,214
I've been in the first grade classroom.

12
00:00:52,214 --> 00:00:55,913
Actually getting to teach has been pretty incredible.

13
00:00:55,913 --> 00:01:04,470
Our program is small enough that you're going to build good relationships with faculty and with your peers.

14
00:01:04,470 --> 00:01:12,734
A lot of our classes, like towards the end before internships, were really fun because we were actually practicing things that you would do with the kids.

15
00:01:12,734 --> 00:01:19,056
But I really do think most of the professors care about you outside of the classroom, and they really do care about you as a person.

16
00:01:19,056 --> 00:01:21,772
Being available even outside of office hours.

17
00:01:21,772 --> 00:01:25,572
A lot of the support comes from their experience as grade school teachers.

18
00:01:25,572 --> 00:01:33,773
They bring that knowledge into your college class by sharing their own personal experiences and saying this is what I did and kind of introducing you to new ideas.

19
00:01:33,773 --> 00:01:38,291
Teachers are needed everywhere, and teachers have such a valuable role in society.

20
00:01:38,291 --> 00:01:45,357
It's awesome knowing that I really could go to New York or I could go to California and most likely find a teaching job.

21
00:01:45,357 --> 00:01:51,401
We have graduates who teach in Arizona, Texas, California, Wyoming, Montana.

22
00:01:51,401 --> 00:02:01,557
With that Colorado license, there's a pathway that's a little bit easier to get that license in another state.

23
00:02:01,557 --> 00:02:06,070
So with all of our programs, we partner with other departments across campus.

24
00:02:06,070 --> 00:02:09,980
That also means that all of our candidates are going to have two advisors here.

25
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:15,302
An advisor in their concentration area, and they're going to have an advisor in education.

26
00:02:15,302 --> 00:02:22,317
They really make it clear through your teaching experience before you graduate that you are always supported.

27
00:02:22,317 --> 00:02:26,863
I feel ready right now because I've been in the classroom and I've been around the kids.

28
00:02:26,863 --> 00:02:29,363
But I've always felt ready because they have gave me the resources and the skills that I know that I need.

